Soft Delete

Suppose someone deletes:

db-password

Without Soft Delete:

❌ Permanently lost.

With Soft Delete:

Deleted Secret

↓

Recover

Recovery is possible within the retention period.

Purge Protection

Even administrators cannot permanently delete protected secrets until the configured retention period expires.

This is useful for compliance.

Enterprise Security Best Practices

✅ Use Managed Identity

✅ Enable Soft Delete

✅ Enable Purge Protection

✅ Use RBAC

✅ Disable Public Network Access (where appropriate)

✅ Use Private Endpoints

✅ Rotate Secrets

